d, it adds the selected work items to the chosen epic(s). The purpose is to provide a clear call-to-action for users to confirm and execute assigning work items to epics.'},jiraEpicSuggestTitleIssues:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-epic-suggest-title-issues",defaultMessage:"I found {count} {count, plural, one {issue that doesn’t have a parent issue} other {issues that don’t have parent issues}}, {andEpics}",description:'Message text displayed in an action card within the AI conversation interface when the AI suggests assigning work items to epics. Shown as the main message text in the action card body. The count placeholder will be substituted with the number of work items found. The ICU MessageFormat plural statement resolves to "issue that doesn\'t have a parent issue" when count is 1, or "issues that don\'t have parent issues" when count is 2 or more. The andEpics placeholder will be substituted with text about suggested epics (from jiraEpicSuggestTitleAndEpics). The purpose is to inform users how many work items were found that could benefit from being organized under epics.'},jiraEpicSuggestTitleAndEpics:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-epic-suggest-title-and-epics",defaultMessage:"and {count, plural, one {an epic} other {some epics}} we could link them to.",description:'Message text displayed as part of the epic suggestion title within the AI conversation interface, indicating how many epics the AI found that could be linked to the work items. Shown as continuation text in the action card body. The count placeholder will be substituted with the number of epics found. The ICU MessageFormat plural statement resolves to "an epic" when count is 1, or "some epics" when count is 2 or more. The purpose is to inform users how many epics the AI has identified that could organize the work items.'},jiraEpicAssignButtonIssueTermRefresh:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-epic-assign-button-issue-term-refresh",defaultMessage:"Add selected work items to {epicCount, plural, one {epic} other {epics}}",description:'Button label displayed on the primary action button in the Jira epic assignment action card within the AI conversation interface (using refreshed terminology). Shown as the text on a button at the bottom of the action card. The epicCount placeholder will be substituted with the number of epics selected. The ICU MessageFormat plural statement resolves to "epic" when count is 1, or "epics" when count is 2 or more. When clicked, it adds the selected work items to the chosen epic(s). The purpose is to provide a clear call-to-action for users to confirm and execute assigning work items to epics.'},jiraIssuesDropdownTitleText:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-issues-dropdown-title-text",defaultMessage:"Select work items to add to epic",description:"Title text displayed above a dropdown or selector component in the Jira epic assignment action card within the AI conversation interface. Shown as a section title or heading. The purpose is to identify the work item selector section, which allows users to select which work items will be added to the suggested epic. This helps users choose which items to organize under the epic."},jiraEpicSuggestSubtitleText:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-epic-suggest-subtitle-text",defaultMessage:"Select the work items you want to add to {epicsCount, plural, one {this epic} other {these epics}}:",description:'Instruction text displayed in the Jira epic assignment action card within the AI conversation interface, guiding users on which work items to select. Shown as instructional text in the action card body. The epicsCount placeholder will be substituted with the number of epics selected. The ICU MessageFormat plural statement resolves to "this epic" when count is 1, or "these epics" when count is 2 or more. The purpose is to guide users to select the work items they want to add to the chosen epic(s).'},jiraEpicSuggestActionCardTitle:{id:"ai-mate.message-actions.jira-epics-suggest.action-card-title",defaultMessage:"Assign work items to epics",description:"Title text displayed at the top of an action card in the AI conversation interface when the AI suggests assigning Jira work items to epics. Shown as the card header title. The purpose is to immediately communicate to the user what action the card represents, which is organizing work items by assigning them to epics."},jiraAssignIssueSuccessMessageText:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-assign-issue-success-message-text",defaultMessage:"OK, I've added those work items to {totalEpics, plural, one {this epic} other {these epics}}:\\n{epicLinks}",description:'Success message displayed in the AI conversation interface after work items have been successfully assigned to epics. Shown as a confirmation message in the chat history. The totalEpics placeholder will be substituted with the number of epics the items were added to. The ICU MessageFormat plural statement resolves to "this epic" when count is 1, or "these epics" when count is 2 or more. The epicLinks placeholder will be substituted with clickable links to the epics in Jira, separated by newlines. The purpose is to confirm the successful assignment and provide immediate access to the epics.'},jiraBulkAssignIssueUnexpectedErrorMessageText:{id:"ai-mate.chat-history.store-assistant.message-actions.jira-bulk-assign-issue-unexpected-error-message-text",defaultMessage:"Something went wrong while assigning work items to epics.",description:"Error message displayed in the AI conversation interface when an unexpected error occurs while assigning work items to epics. Shown as an error message in the chat history or in an error notification. The purpose is to inform the user that the assignment encountered an error and could not be completed, prompting them to try again or check for issues."},jiraAssig